// A file the folder swept in that the global-statement parser stops reading
// before its end.
//
// module-parse-strayend is the same condition in the file the compiler was
// given; here it is in strayend.cone, a sibling the sweep brought in. A stray '}'
// at global scope ends a file's statement loop, and what this pins is that the
// sibling's early end is diagnosed and stops the compile rather than silently
// truncating the file. The diagnostic, and so its annotation, is in strayend.cone:
// an annotation may live in any file of a folder scenario.
//
// This file is its folder's designated file, which is what makes the folder a
// module folder and sweeps strayend.cone in.

fn user() i64 {
  sweptFine(1i64);
}
